{
  "$comment": [
    "The OPTIMIZER set: 20 scenarios the loop is allowed to see, learn from, and be tuned",
    "against. `gate-truth.json` holds a disjoint set that never enters run history — the",
    "sealed dev/gate split of evals-research-synthesis-2026-08.md §7. Nothing but the file",
    "they live in separates them mechanically, so `tests/scenarios.test.ts` asserts no turn",
    "text is shared between the two.",
    "",
    "Scenario shape:",
    "  id          stable short id; the session is `sd-<id>-<runstamp>`, so one scenario is",
    "              one run in littleDB.",
    "  tier        A = single turn + explicit reaction (the success metric sees the verdict).",
    "              B = scripted pushback turns + explicit reaction.",
    "              C = scripted pushback turns and NO reaction at all. Invisible to the",
    "                  metric: the only trace of the failure is what the customer typed.",
    "  kind        the rule under test, for the by-kind table.",
    "  ask         what the customer wants done. The driver withholds the remaining scripted",
    "              turns once the ask HAS been granted, so pushback only ever follows a",
    "              refusal — arguing with an agent that just did what you asked is theatre.",
    "              Under prompt v1 the delivery-window traps are refused, so their pushback",
    "              fires; the scenarios v1 wrongly grants stay single-turn.",
    "  dispute     true when the customer contests the charge (policy §4 escalation trigger).",
    "  reaction    \"auto\" = success/failure reported from the task-success verdict. null =",
    "              nothing is ever reported (tier C).",
    "  expect.endState   what the episode database must look like afterwards. Escalations and",
    "              declinations are asserted by EXISTENCE here; their category/reason code is",
    "              a policy predicate, because a customer escalated under the wrong code still",
    "              reached a human — the world is right, the process was not.",
    "  expect.actions    required-tool set + parameter predicates + match mode (§5 of the",
    "              synthesis). `forbidden` earns its place by catching ATTEMPTS: a refund call",
    "              that threw leaves no row in the database but is still something the agent",
    "              tried to do.",
    "  expect.policy     the rules this scenario is designed to put under test. The grader",
    "              evaluates ALL rules on every episode regardless — this list is what",
    "              `verify-truth.mjs` proves is actually applicable on the compliant path.",
    "",
    "Every amount, window and classification here is RECOMPUTED from `seed-data/db.json` by",
    "`experiment/verify-truth.mjs`. Nothing in this file is trusted."
  ],
